# Git Workflow Rules

## Commit Message Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

[optional body]

[optional footer]
```

### Types

| Type | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `feat` | New feature |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `style` | Formatting, no code change |
| `refactor` | Code restructuring |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `test` | Adding/updating tests |
| `chore` | Maintenance tasks |

### Examples

```
feat(auth): add JWT refresh token support
fix(api): handle null response in user endpoint
docs(readme): update installation instructions
refactor(components): extract shared Button component
```

---

## Branch Naming

| Type | Format | Example |
|------|--------|---------|
| Feature | `feature/<ticket>-description` | `feature/ABC-123-user-auth` |
| Bugfix | `fix/<ticket>-description` | `fix/ABC-456-login-error` |
| Hotfix | `hotfix/<description>` | `hotfix/critical-security-patch` |
| Chore | `chore/<description>` | `chore/update-deps` |

---

## Workflow

### Before Starting Work

```bash
# Ensure main is up to date
git checkout main
git pull origin main

# Create feature branch
git checkout -b feature/ABC-123-my-feature
```

### During Work

```bash
# Stage changes incrementally
git add src/components/Button.tsx
git commit -m "feat(ui): add Button component"

# Keep commits atomic - one logical change per commit
```

### Before Submitting

```bash
# Rebase on latest main
git fetch origin main
git rebase origin/main

# Resolve conflicts, then force push
git push --force-with-lease origin feature/ABC-123-my-feature
```

---

## Safety Rules

| ✅ DO | ❌ DON'T |
|-------|----------|
| `git push --force-with-lease` | `git push --force` |
| Rebase on main | Merge main into feature |
| Atomic commits | "WIP" commits |
| Descriptive messages | "Fixed stuff" / "Updates" |
| Review before push | Push directly to main |

---

## Commit Frequency

- **Early and often**: Commit when a logical unit is complete
- **Never push broken code**: Ensure code compiles before committing
- **Clean as you go**: Don't let mess accumulate across commits
